---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="About — Valentin Backofen" description="About Valentin Backofen" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>

			<p>
				I'm Valentin Backofen — a German-Canadian technology leader based in Montreal. I lead a
				tech factory for a bank-wide digital transformation at one of Canada's largest banks,
				after twenty years of shipping software across agencies, startups, and enterprises.
			</p>

			<p>
				My career started in web development, wound through digital agency leadership, took a
				detour through social gaming entrepreneurship (co-founding QiSports), and landed in
				enterprise architecture. Past clients span Toyota, Air Canada, IKEA, L'Oréal,
				Mastercard, Rogers, and Health Canada. I've shipped code, founded companies, and led
				teams — which means I can cut through technological jargon because I actually understand
				what's beneath it.
			</p>

			<p>
				These days I'm focused on the intersection of agentic AI and banking architecture —
				how autonomous agents change the way we build, operate, and think about software. I
				track the frontier of autonomous coding and banking architecture standards, and I
				believe the next decade of software development will look fundamentally different from
				the last.
			</p>

			<p>
				My North Star, borrowed from John F. Woods: <em>"Always code as if the guy who ends up
				maintaining your code will be a violent psychopath who knows where you live. Code for
				readability."</em> This applies beyond code — it's a philosophy about leaving things
				legible, maintainable, and honest for whoever comes next.
			</p>

			<p>
				I'm multilingual — English and German (native), Norwegian and French (proficient). I'm
				a father of four, and I use a reMarkable Paper Pro as my daily driver for reading and
				notes because e-ink is a deliberate choice for distraction-free work.
			</p>

			<p>
				This blog is where I publish findings from my radar research, project announcements, and
				thoughts that don't fit in a LinkedIn post. You can find me on
				<a href="https://github.com/vevmesteren">GitHub</a> and
				<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/valentinbackofen">LinkedIn</a>.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
